From: multiplayereverything <multiplayereverythingofficial@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 03:31:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] ZooTogether protocol 2: join-in-progress zoo transfer,
 date and pause sync

- Host saves its zoo through SAVE_GAME (save dialog detoured to a fixed path) and streams it in
  32 KB chunks; the client loads it like the main menu's Load Saved Game and enters the game
- State snapshot carries cash, date (SYSTEMTIME), paused flag and intent acks
- Client pause toggles become acked requests; snapshots never undo an unsent toggle
- coop_load_zoo now enters the game (LOAD_FILE, ZTGameMgr::start, hide start screen)
- Lab helpers: coop_layout (placed-entity fingerprint), coop_set_pause, coop_test_shift_date

